    "type": "question",
    "label": "21",
    "prompt": "Find the equation of the normal to the curve $y=(x^2+1)^4$ at $(1,16)$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x+64y-1025=0$",
      "worked": "Using the general power rule,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{dy}{dx}&=4(x^2+1)^3(2x)\\\\\\frac{dy}{dx}&=8x(x^2+1)^3.\\end{align*}$$\nAt $x=1$,\n$$\\begin{align*}m&=8(1)(1^2+1)^3\\\\m&=64.\\end{align*}$$\nThe normal gradient is $m_{\\perp}=-\\frac{1}{64}$. Using $(1,16)$,\n$$\\begin{align*}y-16&=-\\frac{1}{64}(x-1)\\\\64y-1024&=-x+1\\\\x+64y-1025&=0.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
